  "visualizerParams": {
    "title": "Bug Squasher: Total is NaN",
    "language": "html",
    "problemDescription": "The page should show the sum of the doubled numbers, but it shows NaN. The map function does not return anything.",
    "buggyCode": "<p id=\"out\"></p>\n<script>\n  var prices = [5, 10, 15];\n  var withTax = prices.map(function (p) { p * 2; });\n  var sum = withTax.reduce(function (a, b) { return a + b; }, 0);\n  document.getElementById('out').textContent = sum;\n</script>",
    "solution": {
      "code": "<p id=\"out\"></p>\n<script>\n  var prices = [5, 10, 15];\n  var withTax = prices.map(function (p) { return p * 2; });\n  var sum = withTax.reduce(function (a, b) { return a + b; }, 0);\n  document.getElementById('out').textContent = sum;\n</script>",
      "explanation": "A function with curly braces returns undefined unless it has a return statement. map then builds an array of undefined, and adding undefined gives NaN."
    },
